Q.1) Write a Python program to create a DataFrame with the attributes Temperature, Humidity, Wind
Speed, Pressure, and Rainfall. Apply the following data transformation techniques and display
the transformed data:
a)Min-MaxScaling
b)Standardization
c) Normalization

import pandas as pd
from sklearn.preprocessing import MinMaxScaler, StandardScaler, Normalizer
data = {
    'Temperature': [25, 30, 35, 20, 28],
    'Humidity': [60, 70, 80, 50, 65],
    'Wind Speed': [10, 15, 20, 8, 12],
    'Pressure': [1010, 1005, 1000, 1015, 1008],
    'Rainfall': [5, 10, 15, 2, 8]
}
df = pd.DataFrame(data)
minmax = MinMaxScaler()
minmax_data = minmax.fit_transform(df)
standard = StandardScaler()
standard_data = standard.fit_transform(df)
normal = Normalizer()
normal_data = normal.fit_transform(df)
print("Original Data:")
print(df)
print("\nMin-Max Scaling:")
print(pd.DataFrame(minmax_data, columns=df.columns))
print("\nStandardization:")
print(pd.DataFrame(standard_data, columns=df.columns))
print("\nNormalization:")
print(pd.DataFrame(normal_data, columns=df.columns))



Q.2) Create two DataFrames containing information about different mobile phones.
DataFrame 1: Brand, Model, Price, RAM
DataFrame 2: Model, Storage, Battery_Capacity, Operating_System 
Perform the following data transformation techniques:
a) Data Integration by combining the two DataFrames using Model
b) Label Encoding on the Brand attribute of the merged DataFrame
c) One-Hot Encoding on the Operating_System attribute of the merged DataFrame 
Display the original DataFrames, merged DataFrame, and transformed DataFrame.


import pandas as pd
from sklearn.preprocessing import LabelEncoder
df1 = pd.DataFrame({
    'Brand': ['Samsung', 'Apple', 'OnePlus', 'Vivo', 'Xiaomi'],
    'Model': ['S23', 'iPhone15', '12R', 'V29', 'Note13'],
    'Price': [70000, 80000, 45000, 30000, 25000],
    'RAM': [8, 6, 8, 8, 6]
})
df2 = pd.DataFrame({
    'Model': ['S23', 'iPhone15', '12R', 'V29', 'Note13'],
    'Storage': [256, 128, 256, 128, 256],
    'Battery_Capacity': [3900, 3349, 5500, 4600, 5000],
    'Operating_System': ['Android', 'iOS', 'Android', 'Android', 'Android']
})
print("DataFrame 1:")
print(df1)
print("\nDataFrame 2:")
print(df2)
merged = pd.merge(df1, df2, on='Model')
print("\nMerged DataFrame:")
print(merged)
le = LabelEncoder()
merged['Brand'] = le.fit_transform(merged['Brand'])
merged = pd.get_dummies(merged, columns=['Operating_System'], dtype=int)
print("\nTransformed DataFrame:")
print(merged)



